[{:db/id 17592186161979 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ea940e2f-7cf1-5b69-9241-9cde37e5f341"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186360684 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{2}$ is always symmetric.\n\nII. The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n\nIII. If $A$ is a symmetric matrix, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ea940e2f-7cf1-5b69-9241-9cde37e5f341" :question/id #uuid "ea940e2f-7cf1-5b69-9241-9cde37e5f341" :question/math-academy-id "q-140503" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${p}_{12}\\ne {p}_{21},$ we obtain $P\\ne {P}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $R={R}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$Q$ and $R$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2dcd0455-6677-5df3-b08a-01a2a95723e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2dcd0455-6677-5df3-b08a-01a2a95723e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "2dcd0455-6677-5df3-b08a-01a2a95723e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-33ef6a26-6c4e-56d3-8e19-d9dc460624f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13edd389-e8cd-52c8-8f6e-2c34ed7ad05c" "answer-655424c1-b811-5aaf-8538-b1da76023605" "answer-33ef6a26-6c4e-56d3-8e19-d9dc460624f7" "answer-65dc2a15-12f3-5c0d-999e-1bc8c09548b8" "answer-0aa99686-720d-5c83-8792-909de2767703"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13edd389-e8cd-52c8-8f6e-2c34ed7ad05c" :answer/id #uuid "13edd389-e8cd-52c8-8f6e-2c34ed7ad05c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-655424c1-b811-5aaf-8538-b1da76023605" :answer/id #uuid "655424c1-b811-5aaf-8538-b1da76023605" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33ef6a26-6c4e-56d3-8e19-d9dc460624f7" :answer/id #uuid "33ef6a26-6c4e-56d3-8e19-d9dc460624f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65dc2a15-12f3-5c0d-999e-1bc8c09548b8" :answer/id #uuid "65dc2a15-12f3-5c0d-999e-1bc8c09548b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0aa99686-720d-5c83-8792-909de2767703" :answer/id #uuid "0aa99686-720d-5c83-8792-909de2767703" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the matrices are symmetric" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-4147fa8b-5ff8-579d-afae-acd5982a7b2d" :activity/id #uuid "4147fa8b-5ff8-579d-afae-acd5982a7b2d" :activity/title "Symmetric Matrices" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050021 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-850fd871-11f1-5a64-9c68-516ffbeed054" "step-13d711fe-4f91-5fa4-8a59-b8df54fc9061" "step-ae65fa76-f15c-5a90-8603-42143fe53ed6"] :activity/first-step "step-850fd871-11f1-5a64-9c68-516ffbeed054" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-850fd871-11f1-5a64-9c68-516ffbeed054" :step/id #uuid "850fd871-11f1-5a64-9c68-516ffbeed054" :step/content 17592186357611 :step/next "step-13d711fe-4f91-5fa4-8a59-b8df54fc9061" :db/ensure [:step/valid